# Application

- Use Typescript for all
- Use English for all code and documentation
- Run the ``npm run eslint`` to validate and fix the linting based on ``eslint.config.js``.
- Do not implement extra functions rather than defined in the features or prompt.

# Code Style

- Type import must be with ``import { type Typename } from './module';``.
- If all are type, use ``import type { TypeA, TypeB, TypeC } from './module';`.
- Maintain the same functionality but with less code duplication
- Keep all modules skinny
- Type Safety with typescript
- Follow module-based approach (no classes)
- Proper null handling
- Always follow linting from ``eslint.config.js`` configuration
- Uses promise/then instead of async/await
- Documen all function with JTDocs with example
- TypeScript Type: Use type definitions instead of interfaces
- Case: Use pascalCase always
- Use descriptive variable names (eg. isLoading, hasPermission)
- Avoid using ``any`` type.
- Use complete word instead of abbreviation and correct spelling.
- Never user ``for`` loop, use recursive in stead.
- Never use ``while`` loop, use recursive in stead.
- Never exceed 100 characters or columns per line
- When the string is too long, separate lines into array and merge using ``join(' ')`` method.
- Never use legacy or deprecated function, type or property.
- Use quick return.
- Never use ``Promise.all``, use ``promise.then`` only.
- Always clean and remove unused property, parameter, variable and imorted member.
- Too long string example

    ```ts
    const description = [
      'Welcome to the Vibe coding structure.',
      'We need to make sure everthing is formated',
      ---
    ].join(' ');
    ```

## Variable

- Object member always in ``camelCase``.
- Always name it using pascal Case (pascalCase)
- Never user term of ``array``, ``data``, ``info``, ``record`` as suffixing.
- The constant object used for configuration naming is pascaleCase but its member is UPPER_CASE as the following example:

  ```ts
  export const userStatus = {
    LOCKED: 'locked',
    ACTIVE: 'active',
  };
  ```
## Type Declaration

- Use ``type`` instead of ``interface`` if there is not action
- Avoiding using ``any`` as type.
- Naming using ``PascalCase``.
- Type members must be in ``camelCase``.

## Function and calling a function

- Use atomic function concept and approach.
- Function name is pascal Case (pascalCase)
- Each function start with verb.
- Write short function for single purpose, less than 20 instructions.
- If the function returns boolean, use ``isX``, ``canX``, ``hasX``.
- Each function export individually with own export
- Number of function parameters: maximum is 3, which the 3rd is with optional value.

### **No parameter Spread**

- Avoiding using extracted type for parameters, use 

```ts
// DO NOT
const myFuncName = ({ name, age, gender}: User) =>

// DO
const myFunName = (user: User) => {
  const { name,age, gender } = user;
  /* -- function body -- */
}
```

- Long string parameter, need to be declared first, to keep the code clean and easier to read.

```ts
  // [BAD] NOT TO USE THIS WAY
  .then(({ subtitle, phrases }: {
    subtitle: Subtitle;
    phrases: Array<{entryId: number, timeline: string, translatedPhrase: string}>,
  }) => writeExportFile(subtitle, phrases, subtitleId, destinationLanguage))

  // [GOOD] USE THIS

  type Phrase = {
    entryId: number,
    timeline: string,
    translatedPhrase: string,
  };

  type Reesult = {
    subtitle: Subtitle,
    phrases: Phrase[]
  };

  /* --- */
  .then((result: Result) => {
    const { subtitle, phrases } = result;
    return writeExportFile(subtitle, phrases, subtitleId, destinationLanguage);
  });
```

## Avoid Quick return with catch

When using promise/then or try catch, no need use quick return, throw error in stead.

```ts
return findUser(1)
  .then((user: User) => {
    const hasUser = user || false;
    if (!hasUser) throw new Error('User does not exist.');
    return user;
  })
  .catch((error: Error) => {
    const { message } = error;
    logger().error({ action: 'user.get', message });
  });
``

## Nested promise/then

- Use quick return, to make code clean
- The ``throw new Error`` or ``throw`` as quick failed process.
- Try not to have nested ``then``.
- No promise hell is implemented.
- Declare another function and use it to avoid **then hell**.
- Use next ``then`` rather than return another promise

```ts
const processInfo = functionA()
  .then((result) => {
    if (!result) throw new Error('Error');
    return functionB(result);
  })
  .then((resultA) => functionC(resultA));
```

## Implemenation

- Create only required or told function/modules .
- Never create extra function to be used in the future.

## Testing

- Use the standard Jest framework for testing
- Auto generate unit test file located next to the module and suffixed by ``.test.ts``

## Memory Bank

- User-defined feature is located under the ``memory-bank/feature`` folder
- Main feature is defined in the ``memory-bank/feature/index.md`` file
- Never update the content of the user-defined features
- Never generate any content automatically on the user-define features (``memory-bank/feature``).
- Initialize or Update memory bank must strictly follow cursor rules.
- Initialize or update memory bank, need to create the ``feature`` folder if not exist
